# THE TITLE SCREEN - a course nobody plays (SPEC.md 128.23): after the owner's
# sketch (docs/plans/bounce-bonanza/title-sketch.png), its perspective made
# isometric. The window never moves (`view`); the lettering and the key hints
# are ART painted over the picture (title.bba); label 0 is the slot's digit.
# PROVISIONAL: the owner's to refine (128.23.5).
#
# Screen directions: +x is right-down, +y left-down, -x up-left, -y up-right.
#  UR  the upper right platform, 4 units up: the brown tube's exit and the
#      hidden tube's on its back row, the windmill's doorway on its -x edge
#  the PILLAR, the windmill's house, between UR and LS: the windmill's exit is
#      an arch in its +x face at the channel's floor; the RAIL behind UR
#  LS  the strip under the lettering, half a unit up: the brown tube's ENTRY;
#      a step down to it from LL
#  LL  the lower left platform, 1.5 units up, running off the glass to the
#      left: spring 1 at its front edge over the PIT, aimed at LC
#  LC  the lower centre, the front floor, running off the bottom; spring 2 in
#      front of UR's cliff, its power set to land a ball on UR
#  the RAMP from UR's +x edge down to the floor; LR, the row BEHIND it (a ball
#      rolling there is behind the ramp); the HIDDEN tube's mouth past the
#      glass's bottom right corner
course TITLE "Bounce Bonanza"
width 128
origin 512
ball rubber
# story 9.8 (SPEC.md 128.25.20): today's props' families, home RESIDENT (128.25.6.9); and GLASS, home
# FETCH, for the glass bridge over the pit (SPEC.md 128.23.5, the owner 2026-11-17)
uses rotor spring tube glass
title
view 56 124 drop 128
# the title screen's song (song 7, by name): a ONE-SHOT exactly as long as a title demo (BZ_TSTEPS)
music attract

# LC, and the channel in front of UR's cliff; the PIT beside LL, two wide from LS's back wall to the
# bottom of the glass (the owner, 2026-11-16: a corner of LC beside it hid the gap; 2026-11-17: the
# visible strip in front of the pillar taken out too - glass's hidden BRIDGE crosses there now, below)
floor rect 14 12 17 17 flat 2
floor rect 14 9 18 12 flat 2
# the pillar, its back, and the rail behind UR and LR
wall rect 12 7 14 12 flat 9.5
wall rect 12 6 14 7 flat 9
wall rect 12 5 25 6 flat 9
# UR
floor rect 14 6 18 9 flat 6
# the ramp, LR behind it, its foot and the floor in front of it
floor rect 18 7 20 9 ramp x 18 20 6 2
floor rect 18 6 20 7 flat 2
floor rect 20 6 21 11 flat 2
floor rect 18 9 20 11 flat 2
# LR, running off the glass to the right and the bottom
floor rect 21 6 24 11 flat 2
floor rect 17 11 24 17 flat 2
# LR's rails, off the glass: the east one holds the hidden tube
wall rect 24 6 25 18 flat 3
wall rect 14 17 24 18 flat 3
# LS and its back wall, running off the glass to the left (a ball boosted over the brown tube's mouth
# goes on, and off the left side); a STEP down from LL to LS (half a unit each way, which every ball
# rolls), so a ball on LL reaches the mouth (a ramp there laid 6 occluder records in a block, over 4)
floor rect 5 12 12 13 flat 2.5
wall rect 5 11 12 12 flat 3.5
floor rect 9 13 12 14 flat 3
# LL
floor rect 7 14 12 17 flat 3.5

# the brown tube, LS to UR, through the back wall, the pillar and the rail
tube keep 10 12 16 6 via 10 11 via 12 11 via 12 5 via 16 5
# the windmill, UR down through the pillar, out of a doorway in its +x face onto the channel, rolling on
# the way it went in (the owner, 2026-11-16: the exit seen, and no shooting back out to -x)
prop windmill 14 8
tube keep 14 8 14 11 via 13 8 via 13 11 out +x
# the HIDDEN tube, off the glass: its mouth beside the east rail just past the glass's bottom
# right corner (the owner, 2026-11-16: nearer its exit), its body in the rail, up it and along
# the back rail to UR's back row
tube keep 23 11 17 6 via 24 11 via 24 5 via 17 5 out +y
# the GLASS BRIDGE (SPEC.md 128.25.8's glass path; the owner, 2026-11-17): LS carried over the pit at
# LS's height to the channel, where the strip used to be, invisible until a ball rolls onto it - demo
# 3's glass ball, down the step and across; it ends half a step above the channel (no row of the pit
# is level both sides), so its hint is at LS's end, the level one
floor rect 12 12 14 13 flat 2.5
prop glass 12 12
prop glass 13 12
# spring 1 at LL's edge over the pit (the title's springs may stand beside VOID, SPEC.md 128.23.2)
spring 11 15 512
spring 15 9 768

art title.bba 0 0
# label 0, the SLOT: its digit after the plaque's "S  SLOT" (tools/bbtitle.py LABEL_COL, LABEL_ROW)
label 0 11 9 glyphs "123"
start 15 13
